[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API","text":"","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#FastPower.fastpower","page":"API","text":"fastpower(x::Real, y::Real) -> AbstractFloat\n\nCompute an approximate floating-point value of x^y quickly.\n\nfastpower evaluates its approximation through a Float32 logarithm polynomial, trading accuracy for speed. It is intended for nonnegative bases and exponents when a few digits of accuracy are sufficient. Inputs that are not both Real use Julia's ordinary ^ operation.\n\nExamples\n\njulia> using FastPower\n\njulia> fastpower(1.0, 1.0)\n1.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FastPower.fastpower"},{"category":"section","location":"#FastPower.jl","page":"Home","text":"FastPower.jl provides a fast, approximate floating-point power operation for workloads where reduced accuracy is acceptable.\n\nSee the API reference for the supported interface.","title":"FastPower.jl"}]
